# Agent Configuration Rules

## Agent Config Shape

```typescript
type AgentConfig = {
  url: string;        // Required. Agent endpoint URL.
  name: string;       // Required. Display name.
  description?: string;
  protocol: "ag-ui" | "langgraph" | "openai";  // Required. Determines runtime adapter.
};
```

## Environment Variables

- `AGENTS` — JSON object mapping agent IDs to `AgentConfig`. Required.
- `DEFAULT_AGENT` — ID of the default agent. Falls back to first key in AGENTS.
- Agent URLs are server-side only — never expose them to the browser.

## API Route (`/api/agents`)

- Returns agent metadata (id, name, description, protocol) WITHOUT the url field.
- URLs stay server-side. The browser runtime adapter uses `/api/agent-proxy/:id` or
  connects directly only when the agent is explicitly configured as public.

## Validation

- Fail fast at startup if AGENTS is malformed JSON.
- Fail fast if any agent is missing `url` or `protocol`.
- Log warnings for missing optional fields.
